Perfect! All tests are now passing. 

The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` (the second element) instead of `parts[0]` (the first element). Since Python list indices start at 0, the first word is at index 0, not 1.

This caused:
- `test_basic` to fail: returned 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `test_single` to error: tried to access index 1 when only index 0 exists

The fix was simple: changed `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`.
